gm-method/rendering (two 'thing disappears' cull bugs, both from a too-small bounding sphere under per-instance/per-mesh frustum cull): (1) INSTANCED IMPOSTOR billboards pop out near the frustum edge when the InstancedMesh's per-instance cull tests the geometry.boundingSphere * instanceScale and the geo is a unit PlaneGeometry (auto sphere ~0.707) or a zero-area base geo (sphere 0) while the instance is scaled by the object DIAMETER -> the cull sphere is the inscribed/zero sphere, too small, so an on-screen billboard whose CENTER nears the frustum edge culls. FIX: stamp a generous bounding sphere (radius 1.0 so *scale = full diameter, covering the billboard from any angle) on EVERY impostor geo (base + each LOD plane), in BOTH the shared-impostor mesh and the per-species fallback far-LOD. (2) SKINNEDMESH PLAYER/CHAR disappears 'in certain spots': a SkinnedMesh's bounding sphere is computed from the BIND pose, so at certain animation poses/world positions it leaves the frustum and three culls the whole mesh. FIX: set frustumCulled=false on every skinned mesh of an always-near character - AND check EVERY attach path (initial build, re-attach, GLB-fallback) sets it, not just the first (the bug was a re-attach traverse that set castShadow but omitted frustumCulled). GENERAL: when a per-instance/per-mesh frustum cull makes a visible thing vanish, the cull sphere is wrong (partial geo sphere, unit-plane vs scaled billboard, or bind-pose skinned sphere) - stamp the correct whole-object sphere or disable per-mesh frustum cull for always-near objects. Witness: the live mesh's frustumCulled / geometry.boundingSphere.radius via scene.traverse in page.evaluate.